{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment is complete (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), giving a single unimodal RNA baseline with no information about image utility, fusion, or multiprofile effects. Question: Does adding the image modality (resnet50) to the RNA-only model improve validation accuracy? This is the core hypothesis of a multimodal cellular profiling study. config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the most direct and minimal extension of config_001—it holds the RNA encoder, profile setting, and fusion strategy constant while introducing only the image branch with the simplest fusion (concat). This isolates the effect of adding image information with minimal confounding. Why best next: With a limited budget, establishing whether multimodal > unimodal is the highest-value uncertainty to resolve. A clear improvement over 0.485 would justify investing further in multimodal configurations (better encoders, multiprofile, transformer aggregation); a null or negative result would redirect the search toward optimizing the unimodal model or questioning the image pipeline. No other single experiment reduces this central uncertainty as directly."
}

